  "scope": "Independent code review plus native KMB metadata/serialization checks; no repeat of the exhaustive reachable proof or full scoring verification.",
  "review_findings": [
    {
      "topic": "Exact address truth tables",
      "assessment": "Integer bitsets evaluate X/CX/CCX over all 1220 valid addresses without sampling. Forward and reverse input batches are explicitly supplied for all 15 circuits."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Measurement independence",
      "assessment": "Conditional quantum state mutations are rejected; only phase corrections depend on HMR bits. Quantum wire truth tables therefore remain independent of every measurement result."
    },
    {
      "topic": "HMR bit overwrite",
      "assessment": "Each old measurement coefficient must be zero before its classical destination bit is reused. Forgetting that old variable is then valid."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Reset",
      "assessment": "Every R input is required to be identically zero over the full address domain, so resets cannot discard address-dependent information on the proved subspace."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Coherent extension",
      "assessment": "With fixed unconditional HMR count, each branch has input-independent normalization. Zero phase coefficient functions and the same output basis mapping imply the same isometry for arbitrary coherent inputs on the stated subspace, including a reference system."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Inter-circuit classical state",
      "assessment": "Every conditioned CZ must refer to a measurement bit initialized by an HMR in that circuit. No incoming classical bit value is silently assumed to be zero."
    }
  ],
